course: dictionary
lesson: 7899
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word rare has two main meanings. In «collectors may want rare ones», rare means there are only a few of them, so they are special and worth keeping.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you decide. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you have chosen well.
explain: The second meaning is about food. A rare steak is cooked only a little, so it is still red inside. The clue is the word steak nearby. Without a clue like that, you would probably think of the first meaning, so always check the words around it.
fact: Rare has two main meanings: not found often, or cooked only a little (for meat).
fact: «Rare» means not happening often or not found often; there are only a few of it.
fact: «Rare» about meat, especially steak, means cooked only a little, so it is still red inside.
fact: Rare animals may be endangered, like the kakapo, which has very few left in the world.
fact: Chicken and burgers must always be cooked all the way through so they are safe to eat.
exercise: «Some rare birds lay a second egg.» What does rare mean here? | Very loud | Happening every day | Cooked a little | * Not found often, only a few left
exercise: «Collectors may want rare coins.» Why are rare coins valuable? | * There are only a few of them | They are made of gold | They are very big | Shops always sell them
exercise: A steak is described as rare. What does it mean? | Frozen solid | Bought from a rare shop | Cooked very long, dry and brown | * Cooked only a little, still red inside
test: «The kakapo is a rare bird that may be endangered.» What does rare mean here? | * Only a few left in the world | Happening every hour | Very tasty | Very loud
test: Which food must never be served rare, for safety? | Ice cream | * Chicken | Steak | Bread
exam: «Scary news is usually rare, so the world can feel worse than it is.» What does rare mean here? | * Not happening often | Happening often | Very loud | Cooked a little
